---
/* Community & Support - the page behind that entry in the header: the
 * open-source idea and why it is the right model for a framework on SAP, how
 * support works (in the open first), what it stands on, and what a reader can
 * give back. Everything that used to be the "Join the community" section of
 * the home page lives here. */
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const DOCS = "https://abap2ui5.github.io/docs/";
const GITHUB = "https://github.com/abap2UI5/abap2UI5";
const SLACK = "https://abapgit.slack.com/join/shared_invite/zt-46tqufaht-QlrxTzlDqlx85CWbeUnOqg#/shared-invite/email";
const MAIL = "contact@abap2UI5.org";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

/* Support, as a ladder: the open channel first, the maintainers by mail for
 * more. SUPPORT.md in the framework is the source. */
const support = [
  ["Ask in the open", `Write in the <a href="${SLACK}">Slack channel</a> or open an <a href="${GITHUB}/issues">issue on GitHub</a>. Anyone can, at any time, no account with the project needed. Answers stay public, so the next person finds them, and every question makes the documentation and the examples better.`],
  ["Send a pull request", `A fix, a sample, a sentence in the documentation: pull requests are welcome the same way, and every one is reviewed in the open on <a href="${GITHUB}/pulls">GitHub</a>.`],
  ["Need more? Write to us", `Closer cooperation, a workshop, a support arrangement for your organization: write to <a href="mailto:${MAIL}">${MAIL}</a> and plan it together. What is not on offer is an SLA in a contract; what is on offer is a maintainer you can reach.`],
  ["Security reports", `Not in a public issue. Follow <a href="${GITHUB}/blob/main/SECURITY.md">SECURITY.md</a>; a report is acknowledged within three business days.`],
];
/* The community: open source, in the open, and what a reader can give back.
 * Every item is a thing to do, with the place to do it. */
const community = [
  ["Open source, and it stays that way", `MIT licensed since the first commit, every line on <a href="${GITHUB}">GitHub</a>, forks welcome. No company owns it that could close it, change the license or put a release behind a login.`],
  ["We help each other", `Questions go to <a href="${SLACK}">Slack</a> and <a href="${GITHUB}/issues">GitHub</a>, answers stay public. Every question makes the documentation and the examples better for the next person, so ask yours in the open.`],
  ["Built on abapGit and abaplint", `The installation, the tests and every release stand on <a href="https://abapgit.org">abapGit</a> and <a href="https://abaplint.org">abaplint</a>. If abap2UI5 saves you money, consider <a href="https://abapgit.org/sponsor.html">supporting the people behind them</a> too.`],
  ["Add-ons: share yours", `Selection screens, table maintenance, popups, a launchpad KPI: the building blocks live as <a href="https://github.com/abap2UI5-addons">add-ons</a> in the open. The screen you solved for your plant is somebody else's next week.`],
  ["Say what you build", `A post on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/abap2ui5">LinkedIn</a> with #abap2UI5, a talk at your user group, a row under <a href="#who-runs-it">Who runs it</a>: that is how the next decision maker learns it exists.`],
  ["Sponsor the work", `Those zeros are written in somebody's evenings. <a href="${DOCS}resources/sponsor">Sponsoring the contributors</a> says the release you pull next month matters to you.`],
];
---
<Page
  current="community"
  subnav={[["idea", "The idea"], ["support", "Support"], ["community", "Give back"]]}
  title="abap2UI5 - community & support"
  description="abap2UI5 community and support: why it is open source and stays so, how support works in the open, what it stands on, and what you can give back."
>
  <section class="section page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Community &amp; support</p>
      <h1>Open source, in the open, and better with every question</h1>
      <p class="intro">abap2UI5 is open source and stays open source. People help each other in public, because transparency is how a project like this grows. Why that is the right model for a framework on SAP, how support works, what it stands on, and what you can give back.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="idea" aria-labelledby="h-idea">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">The idea</p>
      <h2 id="h-idea">Why open source is the right model for a framework on SAP</h2>
      <div class="split idea">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>A UI framework sits under every screen you build on it. Whoever owns it owns a piece of your landscape: the license, the roadmap, the release cycle, the day it is discontinued. SAP customers know that dependency from both sides, and a second vendor on top of SAP doubles it.</p>
          <p>Open source removes the owner. abap2UI5 is MIT licensed, every line is on GitHub, and the apps built with it are plain ABAP classes in your own system. Nothing can be withdrawn, re-priced or put behind a login, because there is nobody who could. If the project stopped tomorrow, your system would not notice.</p>
          <p>It also changes how the framework gets better. Every question is asked in public and answered in public, so the answer serves the next reader too. Every bug report comes with a class that reproduces it. Every release is tested in the open, on NetWeaver 7.02 and on ABAP Cloud, and anyone can read the test. A vendor asks you to trust; this asks you to look.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="plain idea-list">
          <li><div><b>No owner, no lock-in</b><span>MIT since the first commit. Forks welcome. The apps stay yours, as classes in your system, whatever happens to the project.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><b>Transparent by construction</b><span>Issues, pull requests, releases, the backlog and every test are public on GitHub. Nothing is decided in a room you cannot see.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><b>Built with its users</b><span>The people who run it in production ask, answer and contribute. The question you ask today improves the documentation for the next company.</span></div></li>
          <li><div><b>Standing on open shoulders</b><span>abapGit for installation and versioning, abaplint for every check, UI5 itself for the frontend: open projects all the way down, each with people worth supporting.</span></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt" id="support" aria-labelledby="h-support">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Support</p>
      <h2 id="h-support">In the open first, and more by mail</h2>
      <ol class="week four">{support.map(([b, t]) => <li><b>{b}</b><span set:html={t} /></li>)}</ol>
      <p class="more">→ <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/SUPPORT.md`}>SUPPORT.md</a> in the framework is the source for this page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="community" aria-labelledby="h-community">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Join the community</p>
      <h2 id="h-community">What it stands on, and what you can give back</h2>
      <ul class="strings community">{community.map(([b, t]) => <li><b>{b}</b><span set:html={t} /></li>)}</ul>
      <p class="more">→ Back to <a href={base}>the page for decision makers</a>, or straight to <a href={`${base}#who-runs-it`}>who runs it</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
